      "description": "This introductory-level course offers a comprehensive overview of the fundamental concepts and applications within the fields of aerospace sciences and Earth informatics. Students will explore the evolution of the solar system, delve into the intricacies of Earth's planetary environment, understand the basics of the tools and technologies used to explore the Earth and space, and gain insights into the multidisciplinary field of aerospace science and engineering. The course emphasizes the acquisition and analysis of data from space and other planets, highlighting its significance in understanding our universe and improving life on Earth.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Lecture\nInteractive Tutorial",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "ASEIN & X Double Major PC",
      "academic_org": "ASEIN & X Double Major PC",
      "learning_outcomes": "By the end of this course, students will be able to:\n\n* Explain the processes involved in the formation and evolution of the solar system.\n* Describe the key components and dynamics of Earth's environment and compare them to other planetary environments.\n* Understand the basic tools and technologies used to explore space and Earth.\n* Understand the basic principles of aerospace science and engineering.\n* Apply data analysis techniques to interpret space and planetary data for various applications.\n* Recognize the significance of aerospace technologies in addressing global challenges and advancing scientific knowledge.",
